    "preconditions": {
      "slot": "preconditions",
      "claims": [
        {
          "content": "C2 JU has a Related TN (Track Number) established to which the reference points and geometric areas are to be slaved.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-PC-013",
            "EC-PC-001"
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": "For slaved points and areas, Delta Latitude and 1/Delta Longitude values relative to the Related TN must have been established.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-PC-002",
            "EC-PC-006"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "evidence_card_ids": [
        "EC-PC-013",
        "EC-PC-001",
        "EC-PC-002",
        "EC-PC-006"
      ]
    },
    "trigger": {
      "slot": "trigger",
      "claims": [
        {
          "content": "The trigger for defining slaved reference points and slaved geometric areas relative to a Related TN is the establishment of their position as Delta Latitude and 1/Delta Longitude from the Related TN at the time of the report when the Slaved Indicator is set to value 1. For a slaved Impact Point specifically, the trigger is the identification of a ballistic missile track in the J3.0C5 Related Track Number field.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-TR-001",
            "EC-TR-003"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "evidence_card_ids": [
        "EC-TR-001",
        "EC-TR-003"
      ]
    },
    "main_flow": {
      "slot": "main_flow",
      "claims": [
        {
          "content": "The C2 JU defines the slaved point or area by establishing its position as Delta Latitude 1/Delta Longitude 1 relative to the Related TN at the time of the report and setting the Slaved Indicator to value 1.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-000",
            "EC-MF-015"
          ],
          "step_number": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "The presence or absence of the J3.0C4 continuation word determines if the slaving is relative (included) or true (excluded).",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-015"
          ],
          "step_number": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "To define the slaved geometric area, the C2 JU uses a J3.0I/J3.0E0/J3.0C2 word sequence (or similar variants) and sets the Point/Line/Area Descriptor in the J3.0I word to value 1 (Single Point Area).",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-014"
          ],
          "step_number": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "The C2 JU sets the Square/Circle Switch field to value 1 for square/rectangle or value 2 for circle/ellipse.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-001",
            "EC-MF-014"
          ],
          "step_number": 4
        },
        {
          "content": "The C2 JU sets the Area Major Axis and Area Minor Axis fields equal for squares/circles and unequal for rectangles/ellipses.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-014"
          ],
          "step_number": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "Transmitting a J7.6 (ACT=1) filter description report defines a slaved filter. If the filter is slaved to an existing TN, the TN is reported as TN, Related with Course and Speed set to No Statement; if the J7.6E0 Latitude and Longitude are set to No Statement, the position of TN, Related is used instead. If the filter is to move independently, the TN, Related field is set to No Statement and Course and Speed are specified. Movement of the filter begins at the time of transmission of the J7.6 (ACT=1) filter description report.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-MF-036",
            "EC-MF-037",
            "EC-MF-038",
            "EC-PO-009"
          ],
          "step_number": 6
        }
      ],
      "evidence_card_ids": [
        "EC-MF-000",
        "EC-MF-015",
        "EC-MF-014",
        "EC-MF-001",
        "EC-MF-036",
        "EC-MF-037",
        "EC-MF-038",
        "EC-PO-009"
      ]
    },
    "alternative_flow": {
      "slot": "alternative_flow",
      "claims": [
        {
          "content": "Diverges from Step 1: For an ASW AOP reported in a J3.0 message with Point Type = 7 and Point Amplification = 12, the AOP is not slaved; instead, the C2 JU may transmit a J7.7 Association message to relate or associate the AOP to a track or point.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-AF-002",
            "EC-AF-009"
          ],
          "step_number": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Diverges from Step 1: To relate or associate an ASW AOP to a track or point for which contact has been lost, the C2 JU may transmit a J7.7 Association message.",
          "evidence_refs": [
            "EC-AF-010"
          ],
          "step_number": 2
        }
      ],
      "evidence_card_ids": [
